	quest.02526B34EF26C791.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.04CC377AD9F5B07B.quest_subtitle: "You can get alot of this by washing crushed zinc"
	quest.05B976EA7C244AFC.quest_subtitle: "Gonna need this for the good stuff"
	quest.06BA48DBE3713495.quest_desc: ["You can use a polarizer, or you can be super cool and blast it with lightning"]
	quest.06BA48DBE3713495.quest_subtitle: "There's a right way, and a even more right way"
	quest.09C12548B2EC76AB.quest_subtitle: "The Gold Standard For RPM Control"
	quest.0A21B5CC7028A2DF.quest_subtitle: "ooo shiny"
	quest.0AED133E112A16B2.quest_desc: ["This bad boy can move an entire stack of items at a time"]
	quest.0AED133E112A16B2.quest_subtitle: "The chute she tells you not to worry about"
	quest.0BC631DFEB07BEC3.quest_subtitle: "A 4 block tall blast furnace should be good enough to start off"
	quest.0BC631DFEB07BEC3.title: "Blast Furnace"
	quest.0D618092CDBD9986.quest_desc: [
		"Windmills generate SU based on the number of sails or wool blocks attached to the windmill bearing. For every 8 sails it produces 512 SU, up to a maximum of 8,192 SU with 128 sails. "
		""
		"Note that it ONLY goes up in 512 SU increments, for example: putting 8 sails makes 512 SU, but putting 9 sails still makes 512 SU, not more, so it is reccomended that you put down sails in sets of 8 for the most efficiency. "
		""
		"Also note that if you use sails, you will not need to glue the sails together, unlike wool blocks."
	]
	quest.0D687D9D0EC171F3.quest_desc: ["Copper can be made from washing gravel (same as iron) or using ore excavation"]
	quest.140633537C54BE12.quest_desc: ["A half an hour is a small price to pay for infinite certus quartz"]
	quest.140633537C54BE12.quest_subtitle: "Hope you don't mind a little waiting lol"
	quest.156E9B994039106B.quest_desc: ["Once you have your iron nuggets and andesite, there are three ways to turn it into andesite alloy"]
	quest.1717BFE0BA53BF0A.quest_desc: [
		"Consumption: Machines like presses and mixers consume SU based on how quickly you rotate the shaft within them. Higher rpm equals higher SU usage. The SU usage per rpm is displayed in each machine's description. "
		""
		"These quests only give a brief description and looking at the ponder will demonstrate the uses and details of each machine much more clearly."
	]
	quest.1717BFE0BA53BF0A.quest_subtitle: "and Other Machines"
	quest.1717BFE0BA53BF0A.title: "SU Consumption"
	quest.1B1BACD7324537A2.quest_desc: ["You've got all this slag laying around anyway, might as well use it"]
	quest.1B1BACD7324537A2.quest_subtitle: "You could just mine the stuff, orrr..."
	quest.1B1BACD7324537A2.title: "Nickel and Lead"
	quest.1C5BCD04A4CEAD1A.quest_desc: ["Crafting 2 nuggets and 2 andesite gets you 1 andesite alloy."]
	quest.20415F2F9F931D68.quest_desc: ["Mixes items and/or fluids using a mixer over a basin. Needs a minimum rpm."]
	quest.20415F2F9F931D68.quest_subtitle: "SPIIIIN!"
	quest.2083E650BB40C93D.quest_subtitle: "You need acid to drill this stuff"
	quest.21B2949956EDB3C2.quest_desc: ["Consumes fluid and spouts it onto an item on a depot/belt below."]
	quest.21B2949956EDB3C2.quest_subtitle: "Something about 2 hawks"
	quest.294508BB1C76B21F.quest_desc: [
		"Cuts items sent across it. If used along with a belt, the rotation needs to go in the opposite direction of the belt."
		"Also can do any stonecutting recipe. "
		""
		"&lFilter the item being crafted if you can&r, there are often multiple recipes for any given item. This can be done by right clicking the item you want as a result in the little white box on the cutting surface. "
	]
	quest.294508BB1C76B21F.quest_subtitle: "Saw-stop doesn't exist here so watch your fingers"
	quest.295CB3BE48E9FE12.quest_desc: ["This one is not acheivable early game, but is the most efficient way to get andesite alloy. First you turn the nuggets into iron ingots and melt them into molten iron, mixing that with molten andesite (also made in the foundry basin) will make 2 molten andesite alloy (which then needs to be casted) for every iron nugget and andesite."]
	quest.2ACD6C7D9C589C34.quest_desc: ["Brass is an alloy made from mixing molten zinc and molten copper together and then casting the result."]
	quest.2ACD6C7D9C589C34.title: "Brass Alloying"
	quest.2C2312D2343F54B7.quest_desc: [
		"First things first, if you want to know how any specific block works in Create, check its ponder by holding W on the item. This will give a detailed render of how it is used and it will be much more help than looking at these quests."
		""
		"Now, to begin:"
		"&lSTRESS UNITS&l"
		"Stress units (or SU) is the energy system that Create uses, with certain blocks consuming SU and others that can generate it."
		""
		"Transmission: In order to transfer SU from one place to another, you use shafts, cogwheels, and gearboxes. Shafts go straight and gearshifts can transmit SU in 4 directions."
	]
	quest.2C2312D2343F54B7.quest_subtitle: "Let's Get Started!"
	quest.2C2312D2343F54B7.title: "Create Basics"
	quest.2D6F5CDD49B7AA9C.quest_subtitle: "I suggest getting a couple stacks of this stuff"
	quest.30128726582FD3C7.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.30128726582FD3C7.quest_subtitle: "The fancy redstone coating adds two zeros to the price tag"
	quest.301BA99F0CB16020.quest_desc: [
		"Waterwheels generate constant SU as long as there is flowing water touching any part of the waterwheel. (The small makes 256 SU and the large makes 512 SU). "
		""
		"Note that the small waterwheel spins twice as fast(8 rpm) as the large waterwheel(4 rpm), which can be usefull early game to speed up your machines a bit more."
	]
	quest.30AA015085797F0B.quest_desc: [
		"Works like a crafting table, but slower and worse, but has special crafting recipes exclusive to it. It is modular and only needs as many crafters as items the recipe requires (you need to make sure all crafters are connected, this will use more crafters to acheive this if it is needed). All crafters also need to point in a collective direction, meeting at a singular output."
		""
		"(The ponder demonstrates this better if this doesnt make sense)"
	]
	quest.30AA015085797F0B.quest_subtitle: "You'd think being mechanical would make it better"
	quest.32C7FC63AF3447EE.quest_desc: [
		"Many blocks in create can be encased, such as cogs, shafts, pipes, and belts. Due to the addon mod: Create Encased, you can encase nearly any create block with any create casing. Encasing blocks is usually cosmetic and does not consume the casing, but there are some situations where it is quite useful."
		""
		"Encasing cogs is very useful for making compact builds as it hides the shaft of the cog if it is not connected to anything, allowing for cogs to stack on top of eachother."
		""
		"Encasing pipes can be used to lock the configuration of a pipe. This stops any other pipes from making unwanted connections. (this can also be acheived using the screwdriver item)"
	]
	quest.32C7FC63AF3447EE.title: "Encasing"
	quest.34E070299A1E13FA.quest_subtitle: "A little bonus, it's on the house"
	quest.37CC7D8DFB6B6652.quest_subtitle: "Needs a Blast Furnace"
	quest.37FFB8DB387FDB35.quest_subtitle: "Its basically free after you get the first one"
	quest.38BC826014653A10.quest_desc: ["You wont need much for this chapter but you can take a peak at the next chapter to see about how to automate lead and nickel. "]
	quest.38BC826014653A10.quest_subtitle: "Some Lead Required"
	quest.397CD9408D8659B6.quest_desc: ["Presses items and/or fluids using a press over a a basin."]
	quest.397CD9408D8659B6.quest_subtitle: "Bonking so good they made another one"
	quest.397F1E4727ADF9E3.quest_subtitle: "Easier than making a skeleton farm, I think..."
	quest.399B067B48D4677C.quest_desc: ["These are nice for putting all of your liquid catalysts in to contain them"]
	quest.399B067B48D4677C.title: "Catalysts"
	quest.3B045CB00003B647.quest_desc: ["Presses items on the ground beneath it or on a depot beneath it. Pretty self-explainitory"]
	quest.3B045CB00003B647.quest_subtitle: "BONK!"
	quest.3FFC2F8562204815.quest_subtitle: "Nice for symmetrical building"
	quest.40434A8C50067417.quest_desc: [
		"Cobblestone can be turned into many different item through various combinations of crushing and washing and smelting. "
		"It can be crushed into gravel, and then sand, both of which can be turned into many other products. In the beginning, gravel can be washed to make flint, iron, and copper."
	]
	quest.40434A8C50067417.quest_subtitle: "The Answer to Life, The Universe, And Everything"
	quest.40434A8C50067417.title: "Cobblestone Generation"
	quest.412E7BB5A416D47C.quest_desc: ["Generation: Blocks that generate SU are windmills, waterwheels, steam engines, and the fueled engines from TFMG(they are in a league of their own and won't be discussed in this quest tab. "]
	quest.41AC18035B22AE97.quest_subtitle: "Good for distribution and collection of items"
	quest.41CEF7A3D6CE35A3.quest_subtitle: "Finally..."
	quest.42293018DE870E8D.quest_subtitle: "Don't worry you only need one"
	quest.434363C58B6C8A1B.quest_desc: ["You can make more endstone using levitite. This creates a positive loop that leads to the generation of endstone and levitite at the cost of only zinc."]
	quest.434363C58B6C8A1B.title: "Endstone/Levitite Loop"
	quest.44C3FA5A18CD29E0.quest_desc: ["Deploys and item onto another item on a depot/belt beneath it. This consumes the item in the deployers hand. Can also place blocks and attack mobs."]
	quest.44C3FA5A18CD29E0.quest_subtitle: "Does all the handy work you don't want to"
	quest.4677AC77B24C5064.quest_desc: ["The resulting molten brass needs pumped into a casting basin and is then cooled into heated ingots. Those heated ingot can be dropped into water to be instantly cooled into normal brass ingots. Also, in order to get molten zinc/copper, you need to melt the repective ingot in a heated foundry basin."]
	quest.4677AC77B24C5064.title: "Casting the Brass"
	quest.485DBAF8764766A9.title: "Mixing"
	quest.4C0583E951ED8616.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.4EF712572A9A1C30.quest_subtitle: "Made from distilling naptha and processing the products"
	quest.5342D12C89C5BD16.quest_desc: ["A little crusher. Can be powered from a cog interlocking with the mill, or from a shaft from below."]
	quest.5342D12C89C5BD16.quest_subtitle: "Crushing"
	quest.551BB0BFC792880B.quest_desc: ["It is highly reccomended that you experiment with reactor setups in a creative world, because if the fuel assembly gets too hot and goes super critical then it goes super boom."]
	quest.551BB0BFC792880B.quest_subtitle: "Be seriously careful with this stuff"
	quest.55E06DC488BBE2B3.title: "Pathway To Nuclear"
	quest.5A32B09DE04B593E.quest_subtitle: "(still only within 5 blocks)"
	quest.5A32B09DE04B593E.title: "Paid Lightning"
	quest.5CEEBEDCDFA33D01.quest_desc: ["Chorus can be automated by cutting down chorus trees with a saw and pressing the resulting chorus fruit into blocks and water them to get chorus flowers that you can replant."]
	quest.5E4DFEB1BEAB390B.quest_desc: [
		"Heat is made by blaze burners and basic burners. Basic burners can only acheive low heat normally, needing a max-rpm fan directed at it to maintain regular heat (this also consumes fuel faster). Blaze burners can make regular heat by default, also needing solid fuel. When blaze burners are fed blaze cakes, they become superheated, which is a requirement for some recipes and also makes steam engines more powerful."
		""
		"Blaze burners are made by right-clicking a blaze or a blaze-spawner with an empty blaze burner."
	]
	quest.5E4DFEB1BEAB390B.quest_subtitle: "So hot it makes a dragon wanna retire, man"
	quest.614F4BD59C2EB766.quest_subtitle: "yummers"
	quest.62502713ED5D4AA9.quest_desc: ["Mixing 1 nugget and 1 andesite in a basin makes 1 andesite alloy"]
	quest.63D33F15C859FBE1.quest_desc: ["Polishes items when you put the sandpaper in your offhand and hold right-click the item you want to polish. Can also be put in a deployer to quickly polish items"]
	quest.63D33F15C859FBE1.quest_subtitle: "idk what joke to make here"
	quest.64832D20F7BEF53B.quest_desc: [
		"The only way to turn magnetic alloy into magnets in the beginning is by striking it with lightning, which is a pain in the butt so heres one lightning, on the house. "
		""
		"Keep in mind, this lightning strikes ALL items in a 5 block radius, so don't have anything important around."
	]
	quest.64832D20F7BEF53B.quest_subtitle: "(only within 5 blocks)"
	quest.65EDFA6368867BDE.quest_desc: ["Aeronautics is a mod that adds physics simulation to Minecraft. "]
	quest.65EDFA6368867BDE.title: "Aeronautics Basics"
	quest.697791ED7A5B4F74.quest_desc: ["Iron is made from washing gravel"]
	quest.697D3C47C0C7CD3A.quest_subtitle: "What kind of tech modpack would this be without oil processing?"
	quest.6C9F6ED13A99B014.quest_desc: ["Zinc is generated from ore excavation drills or by mining its ore."]
	quest.6EBCDBDA4C63F741.quest_desc: ["The condition is that the chunks that its in have to be loaded btw."]
	quest.6EBCDBDA4C63F741.quest_subtitle: "Infinite Range! (some conditions may apply)"
	quest.70B73294857094C1.quest_desc: [
		"[ \"Steam Engines can generate massive amounts of SU but needs its \", { \"text\": \"blaze burners\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"5E4DFEB1BEAB390B\" } }, \" to be fueled(anything that fuels a furnace works) and water to be pumped into the boiler using fluid pumps.\" ]"
		""
		"Steam Engines can be made in various sizes or \"levels\" and are constructed from three main parts: the boiler, which is built out of fluid tanks, the steam engines, which determines how much SU is extracted, and the blaze burners, which generate heat for the boiler. "
		""
		"Cont. on next page..."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The boilers level is determined by the lowest of three factors: heat, size, and water. For example if you have a large boiler and plenty of heat, but not enough water, then the steam engine will not produce the maximum amount of SU as it could. Experimenting with these three factors is the best way to get a feel for the \"level\" system. "
		""
		"The level number determines how many steam engines you need, with level 1 needing one and level 18 needing 18. Steam engines at maximum power generate 16,384 SU."
		""
		"The minimum size (level 1) is four fluid tanks, one steam engine, and one blaze burner. The maximum size is level 9 (54 tanks) for normal heating or level 18 (108 tanks) if you are superheating."
	]
	quest.70DD17B16E50D077.quest_subtitle: "add recipes and get that one texture pack"
	quest.7126751C7CC05ACC.quest_desc: ["Andesite is made from compacting flint and gravel"]
	quest.715D20C0D833733A.quest_desc: [
		"Fans blow air thorugh a medium to affect items in front of them. There are four kinds of blowing: Washing, Blasting, Smoking, and Haunting."
		"Washing needs water in front of the fan"
		"Blasting needs lava. It also can do all furnace recipes without needing fuel"
		"Smoking needs fire or a campfire. It can do all smoking recipes similiarly to blasting"
		"Haunting needs soul fire or a soul campfire."
	]
	quest.715D20C0D833733A.quest_subtitle: "Get your mind out of the gutter"
	quest.72E7A34347FBF410.quest_desc: ["Some recipes like the precision mechanism require an assemply-line-esque process to make them. These recipes contain multiple steps and often require multiple different machines. Note that some recipes need multiple loops, so take that into account when automating."]
	quest.72E7A34347FBF410.quest_subtitle: "Some Assembly Required"
	quest.72E7A34347FBF410.title: "Sequential Crafting"
	quest.75DF01889B7F4D9F.quest_desc: ["Automated brewing is more or less the same as normal potion brewing, where you start with water and add ingredients to the basin one at a time."]
	quest.75DF01889B7F4D9F.quest_subtitle: "Brewing can be automated with mixers"
	quest.760FE73005BA64C1.quest_subtitle: "Drop it into the abyss to absorb its essence"
	quest.7747EEDF16D76A3B.quest_desc: ["Big crusher. Insert items from above and it spits out the result below, can process a stack of items at a time. Must be built in pairs and rotated in opposite directions. Also, becareful not to slip into the business end, you won't like what happens."]
	quest.7747EEDF16D76A3B.quest_subtitle: "Crushing 2: Electric Boogaloo"
